      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "STRINGER LASS (5) gets the nod after a sharp first-up second at Young, beaten a nose by Happy Joy as the odds-on favourite. She was plain in F NMT1W/TS company before the break, but that latest run is the strongest exposed maiden form here and she should be fitter second-up. IDEAL LILLY (7) is the main danger among the raced runners: her seventh at Riverina Paceway reads better than it looks, beaten only seven and a half metres in a 1:57.6 mile rate, though the 15-start maiden record is a concern. WILLSACE (2) is a player on debut after winning a Coolamon trial by 10m for a strong Albury stable, and that trial gives him a genuine winning profile if he handles race pressure. TOUCH OF REALITY (11) has placed often enough to matter and her gallop last start gives her a forgiveness angle, but she needs cleaner manners after also having a score-up issue two starts back.",
